From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] local: watchdog: dev: log init's armed handover at notice, not crit

With RebootWatchdogSec working (0241), every shutdown prints three

  watchdog: watchdog0: watchdog did not stop!

at KERN_CRIT, which the console shows even with quiet. All three come from
systemd closing /dev/watchdog0 without the magic character on purpose, so
the watchdog stays armed across an exec: PID 1 -> systemd-shutdown,
systemd-shutdown -> the sd-shutdown exitrd, and the exitrd's
systemd-shutdown before reboot(). Each runs as PID 1.

Log a PID 1 close at notice instead. It stays in dmesg and the journal but
drops below the quiet console level. Any other process closing an armed
watchdog, such as a watchdog daemon dying, still logs at crit. The ping and
the worker update after the message are unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
index d789500..aa1737c 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #include <linux/miscdevice.h>	/* For handling misc devices */
 #include <linux/module.h>	/* For module stuff/... */
 #include <linux/mutex.h>	/* For mutexes */
+#include <linux/sched.h>	/* For current/is_global_init */
 #include <linux/slab.h>		/* For memory functions */
 #include <linux/types.h>	/* For standard types (like size_t) */
 #include <linux/watchdog.h>	/* For watchdog specific items */
@@ -960,7 +961,15 @@ static int watchdog_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 
 	/* If the watchdog was not stopped, send a keepalive ping */
 	if (err < 0) {
-		pr_crit("watchdog%d: watchdog did not stop!\n", wdd->id);
+		/*
+		 * systemd as init closes without the magic character on purpose,
+		 * to keep the reboot watchdog armed across each exec of its
+		 * shutdown chain. Only an unexpected close is critical.
+		 */
+		if (is_global_init(current))
+			pr_notice("watchdog%d: watchdog did not stop!\n", wdd->id);
+		else
+			pr_crit("watchdog%d: watchdog did not stop!\n", wdd->id);
 		watchdog_ping(wdd);
 	}
 
